{"name":"Bridesmaid","hex":"#fae6df","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bridesmaid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman who attends a bride during her wedding ceremony, as part of the main wedding party.","A person or team that perennially finishes well, but never first."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act as a bridesmaid for; to attend a bride during her wedding ceremony."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridesmaid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bridesmaid","blocks":[{"text":"Bridesmaids are members of the bride's party at Western wedding ceremonies. A bridesmaid is typically a young woman and often the bride's close friend or relative. She attends to the bride on the day of a wedding or marriage ceremony. Traditionally, bridesmaids were chosen from unwed young women of marriageable age."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridesmaid","wikidata":"Q902435"},{"title":"Bridesmaid (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bridesmaid are an instrumental stoner rock band from Columbus, Ohio consisting of two bass players and two drummers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridesmaid_(band)","wikidata":"Q85748903"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Lehnga.jpg/500px-Lehnga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Lehnga.jpg/500px-Lehnga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Four bridesmaids wearing gagra cholis, the traditional dress of North India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALehnga.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Bridesmaid_and_junior_bridesmaid-crop.jpg/330px-Bridesmaid_and_junior_bridesmaid-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Bridesmaid_and_junior_bridesmaid-crop.j